      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "NOMORENIGHTSHIFT (6) has settled well back before making late inroads in vain in his two runs this time in work. Drops back from open company to a BM82 under the same weight. Fitter now and is a winner at his only run here on home soil. Perfectly placed to turn things around. FLAMBOYANT LAD (9) travelled midfield but struggled under pressure in the straight when resuming in a Rosehill Highway over 1300m last time out. Deserves another chance down in the weights with the blinkers back on. TAINUI (3) shouldered 60kgs and found it tough first-up at Newcastle over 1250m recently. Drops 3kgs and gets out to a preferable distance. One of the better chances. CRAVING MAGIC (2) hasn't landed a blow in five runs this prep, all on the Canberra Acton track. The rating suggest this is a winnable race so keep him safe. LOCKDOWN GAMBLE (1) finished third in this grade at Dubbo three back and has struggled in better races since. Can bounce back.",
